{"id":"torrey:language","source":"torrey","name":"Language","slug":"language","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Of all mankind one at first — Ge 11:1,6.","refs":[["Gen",11,1,11,1],["Gen",11,6,11,6]]},{"text":"Speech. — Mr 14:70; Ac 14:11.","refs":[["Mark",14,70,14,70],["Acts",14,11,14,11]]},{"text":"Tongue. — Ac 1:19; Re 5:9.","refs":[["Acts",1,19,1,19],["Rev",5,9,5,9]]},{"text":"A punishment for presumption, &c. — Ge 11:2-6.","refs":[["Gen",11,2,11,6]]},{"text":"Originated the varieties in. — Ge 11:7.","refs":[["Gen",11,7,11,7]]},{"text":"Scattered men over the earth. — Ge 11:8,9.","refs":[["Gen",11,8,11,8],["Gen",11,9,11,9]]},{"text":"Divided men into separated nations. — Ge 10:5,20,31.","refs":[["Gen",10,5,10,5],["Gen",10,20,10,20],["Gen",10,31,10,31]]},{"text":"Great variety of, spoken by men — 1Co 14:10.","refs":[["1Cor",14,10,14,10]]},{"text":"Ancient kingdoms often comprehended nations of different — Es 1:22; Da 3:4; 6:25.","refs":[["Esth",1,22,1,22],["Dan",3,4,3,4],["Dan",6,25,6,25]]},{"text":"Hebrew. — 2Ki 18:28; Ac 26:14.","refs":[["2Kgs",18,28,18,28],["Acts",26,14,26,14]]},{"text":"Chaldea. — Da 1:4.","refs":[["Dan",1,4,1,4]]},{"text":"Syriack. — 2Ki 18:26; Ezr 4:7.","refs":[["2Kgs",18,26,18,26],["Ezra",4,7,4,7]]},{"text":"Greek. — Ac 21:37.","refs":[["Acts",21,37,21,37]]},{"text":"Latin. — Lu 23:38.","refs":[["Luke",23,38,23,38]]},{"text":"Lycaonian. — Ac 14:11.","refs":[["Acts",14,11,14,11]]},{"text":"Arabic, &c. — Ac 2:11.","refs":[["Acts",2,11,2,11]]},{"text":"Egyptian. — Ps 84:5; 114:1; Ac 2:10.","refs":[["Ps",84,5,84,5],["Ps",114,1,114,1],["Acts",2,10,2,10]]},{"text":"Of some nations difficult — Eze 3:5,6.","refs":[["Ezek",3,5,3,5],["Ezek",3,6,3,6]]},{"text":"The term barbarian applied to those who spoke a strange — 1Co 14:11.","refs":[["1Cor",14,11,14,11]]},{"text":"A gift of the Holy Spirit. — 1Co 12:10.","refs":[["1Cor",12,10,12,10]]},{"text":"Promised. — Mr 16:17.","refs":[["Mark",16,17,16,17]]},{"text":"Given on the day of Pentecost. — Ac 2:3,4.","refs":[["Acts",2,3,2,3],["Acts",2,4,2,4]]},{"text":"Followed receiving the gospel. — Ac 10:44-46.","refs":[["Acts",10,44,10,46]]},{"text":"Conferred by laying on of the apostles’ hands. — Ac 8:17,18; 19:6.","refs":[["Acts",8,17,8,17],["Acts",8,18,8,18],["Acts",19,6,19,6]]},{"text":"Necessary to spread of the gospel. — Ac 2:7-11.","refs":[["Acts",2,7,2,11]]},{"text":"A sign to unbelievers. — 1Co 14:22.","refs":[["1Cor",14,22,14,22]]},{"text":"Sometimes abused. — 1Co 14:2-12,23.","refs":[["1Cor",14,2,14,12],["1Cor",14,23,14,23]]},{"text":"Ceased when the written Bible completed. — 1Co 13:8-10.","refs":[["1Cor",13,8,13,10]]},{"text":"Antiquity of engaging persons for. — Ge 42:23.","refs":[["Gen",42,23,42,23]]},{"text":"A gift of the Holy Spirit. — 1Co 12:10.","refs":[["1Cor",12,10,12,10]]},{"text":"Most important in the early church. — 1Co 14:5,13,27,28.","refs":[["1Cor",14,5,14,5],["1Cor",14,13,14,13],["1Cor",14,27,14,27],["1Cor",14,28,14,28]]},{"text":"The Jews punished by being given up to people of a strange. — De 28:49; Isa 28:11; Jer 5:15.","refs":[["Deut",28,49,28,49],["Isa",28,11,28,11],["Jer",5,15,5,15]]}],"refCount":54}
